Fixed in `tokio-stream/src/stream_map.rs:687`:

```rust
fn size_hint(&self) -> (usize, Option<usize>) {
    let mut ret: (usize, Option<usize>) = (0, Some(0));

    for (_, stream) in &self.entries {
        let hint = stream.size_hint();

        ret.0 = ret.0.saturating_add(hint.0);

        match (ret.1, hint.1) {
            (Some(a), Some(b)) => ret.1 = a.checked_add(b),
            (Some(_), None) => ret.1 = None,
            _ => {}
        }
    }

    ret
}
```

- Lower bound saturates at `usize::MAX` — a hint, not a promise, so clamping is the right degradation.
- Upper bound uses `checked_add`, collapsing to `None` (unknown) on overflow. Once `None`, later entries hit the `_ => {}` arm and it stays `None`.
- The accumulator needed an explicit `(usize, Option<usize>)` annotation: previously inference flowed in through `+` with `hint.0`; with method calls the integer literals became ambiguous.

This matches the existing `merge_size_hints` helper at `tokio-stream/src/stream_ext.rs:1216`, which already had these semantics — `StreamMap` was the odd one out with raw `+`.

Tests: `size_hint_overflow` now passes, and the whole `tokio-stream` suite is green (28 in `stream_stream_map`, all other targets passing).
